@1 = ~Recently, it's been difficult to come by decent honey in Ulgoth's Beard. The wet weather ruined the hives, and what little the beekeepers have collected has already been bought up. My customers are getting restless. If you bring me a jug, I'll pay you sixty-five gold pieces for it. I can still spare some grain, if you need any.~
@2 = ~Let me see what you have for sale.~
@3 = ~I have some honey. Will you pay 65 gold pieces?~
@4 = ~Maybe another time.~
